<title>USA: NYC plans $775 mln bond sale for January 14.</title>
<headline>NYC plans $775 mln bond sale for January 14.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York City has scheduled its $775 million refunding of taxable and tax-exempt bonds for January 14, said a city official on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're now aiming for January 14,&quot; said the city official, who declined to be named.</p>
<p>The refunding includes the city's first-ever issue of floating rate taxable debt for European markets, a $300 million sale that will be senior-managed by Goldman Sachs.</p>
<p>--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654</p>
</text>
